{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/441409-ghosts-and-such","id":441409,"title":"Ghosts and such...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Geist: The Sin-Eaters"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-14T09:25:40-07:00","id":441409,"title":"Ghosts and such...","content":"I was pondering on Ghosts and I wondered on the theories behind them. I'm still not 100% sure on what exactly they are when it comes to the question of souls. This is perhaps more of a GMC subject, though I think the topic is fitting for this board.<br /> Are they souls of the departed,.. Or are they sort of memories left behind that clung to some unfulfilled purpose, or perhaps a part of the soul left behind due to unfinished business?<br /> <br /> Also can someone who is soulless (not a Promethean or similar, I mean someone like a Mortal that has the Condition of it) generate a ghost if they die with unfinished business to attend to? Such things may potentially tie into Mummy, what with it's Lucid Dead Numen and such... I'm not sure though.<br /> <br /> Also, whats the thoughts on where potentially a Ghost may Pass On to... Would it be possible that a ghost reaches the realm of Stygia in the Supernal? Or do you think that is where a destroyed ghost may end up, due to the shades and spectres of that realm?<br /> I tend to think of the Underworld as having a similar purpose to the one in Wraith, as an area to help ghosts pass on and keep the balance of souls moving along, though it's been some time since I've read through Book of the Dead and I'm not sure now really.<br /> <br /> So, what are your opinions on this subject? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T12:01:07-07:00","id":441676,"title":"","content":"They're very definitely not uniformly souls, much as rumors about ancestor spirits and Lunes in Werewolf don't signify that all spirits are souls.<br /> <br /> Promethean 1e Core includes mention of ghosts of previous Prometheans on a list of story ideas an example ST jots down in its Storytelling chapter, Book of the Dead introduced a mechanic that deposits the Created in the Underworld upon their first death which Matt McFarland's explicitly carried over to 2e as a universal milestone, and nowhere in the last three and a half gamelines I've read has anything come up to indicate that ghosts only come from ensouled beings.<br /> <br /> Dave Brookshaw has also pointed out that ghosts are semi-psychic in nature and that there are supernatural means of making ghosts from people who are still alive.<br /> <br /> Geist's mention of how geister might be something else exploiting a ghost's memories and ties to the mortal world to fulfill an agenda is an aspect I've hooked into the inferred necessity of very old ghosts exploiting younger ghosts to get back to Earth (younger ghosts can still manifest and communicate with the living, after all) and similarly tied to <a href=\"http://wonsab.tumblr.com/post/67932522921/spitballing-on-the-nature-of-ghosts-and-gods\" target=\"_blank\">chthonians</a> through similarities between Fae Charlatans and the necessity of vampiric Touchstones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T12:04:23-07:00","id":441681,"title":"","content":"As always when it comes to a Geist game, I haven't setteled on any hard and fast metaphysics.<br /> The mortal Necromancers general believe it is the nothing but the fragmentet memory of the person given unnatural life due to our shared memory of that individual. Really just a thought-form given life purely by our own wills. They partically use this line of reasoning as an excuse for their abusive behavior towards ghosts, but they claim to have reasonable evidence to support it.<br /> Some Sin-Eaters even agree with them. This is supported by how a persons ghost can change by how society at large percieves him. Think of the ghost of Jack The Ripper, who has become something akin to a god of murder, because thats how society percieves him.<br /> <br /> Other Sin-Eaters believe that Ghosts are literally the soul of the dead person, freed of the body which previously forced the world to remember and appriciate them. Now that they've been deprived of that body, its everyones job to give them a ghostly body with which to sustain themselves long enough for them to move on. Kinda like how you would throw a homeless man some spare change, to get him back on his feet. This is supported by how certain Sin-Eaters and mortal Necromancers can unshackle their souls and wander about as ghostly reflections of themselves, while their bodies lie in a comatose state.<br /> <br /> Some occultists believe a ghost is neither of those things, but rather a persons magical essence freed of the restraints of his body, to take whatever form it desires. This is supported by how certain Awakened Ghosts seem to retain their mystical abillities, and some might even grow more powerful in death than they ever were in life. A Geist then, is merely an occultist merging his own magical essence with an archetypical concept of death, in a gambit to gain an increased measure of controle over said aspect. A Sin-Eater might then be that occultists attempt to reverse his own death, and become alive again. This is supported by the Geister who try to cruelly subjugate the mind of the Sin-Eater and gain full control of the body.<br /> <br /> A few ragged and half-insane people whisper that its actually a cruel parasitic <i>thing </i>from somewhere deep down in the Underworld come crawling up to wear the ethereal essence of the dead person as a shroud. Thats why a newly born ghost mostly repeads its own death or some menial task endless in a cycle. The fragment of the dead persons mind if desperately trying to fight the alien intrusion, clinging to what it faintly remembers it once did or the few painful moments that it remembers that its mind and body were still wholly its own. By this admission, Geister are the next evolutionary stage of this unliving parasite. It has wholly mastered the ghosts etheric essence, and stepped its game up to attempting to overtake a living host. As its power increases, the Deathlords of the Underworld notice the dreadful monster wearing the human skin-suit, and attempts to drag back down below, before its insidious pressence grows too powerful. Thats why a Sin-Eater with Psyche above 5 must spend some time in the Underworld occationally.<br /> <br /> This is mostly how I like to organize my metaphysics in Geist games. Just like the Krewes themselves, the truth should be a mish-mash of differing opinions and labyrinthine half-truth.<br /> Thats my opinion, anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T19:21:09-07:00","id":442083,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the replies already both! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Yeah, having Prometheans end up at a River in the Underworld does seem to show that ghosts are at least not purely souls and are more likely, as mentioned (though feel free to correct or iterate your own thoughts to clarify) a kind of psychic memory form of the person (I'm once again pulled to thinking about Wraiths for this) or that they are the magical essence held within a person. Corpus seems to be made of Plasm, which holds Essence... I'm not an expert when it comes to Mortals and Essence/Ephemera though. I'm leaning kind of on that a ghost is some kind of magical astral shade of the person it originates from though... As mentioned that Mages can make a ghost from a person that's still alive.<br /> <br /> This I suppose asks the question that if a Mage makes a ghost from a living person and they die and have unfinished business... Do they leave behind a ghost for that and now there are two ghosts of the same person?<br /> <br /> I love the idea of the Chthonians btw... I like how they are likely the Old Gods of the Underworld and that the Deathlords are high ranked Underworld dwellers. These are two dwellers of the Underworld I've wanted to know more about for a while now, along with the Kerberos, of course. With the Cthonic Beast being linked to The Beast and possibly Cthonians, could it be that Inferno dwells down low enough in the Underworld?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Some occultists believe a ghost is neither of those things, but rather a persons magical essence freed of the restraints of his body, to take whatever form it desires. This is supported by how certain Awakened Ghosts seem to retain their mystical abillities, and some might even grow more powerful in death than they ever were in life. A Geist then, is merely an occultist merging his own magical essence with an archetypical concept of death, in a gambit to gain an increased measure of controle over said aspect. A Sin-Eater might then be that occultists attempt to reverse his own death, and become alive again. This is supported by the Geister who try to cruelly subjugate the mind of the Sin-Eater and gain full control of the body. </div> </div> </div>That seems quite legit and the closest in my mind, given my other thoughts and brain splurging above. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As its power increases, the Deathlords of the Underworld notice the dreadful monster wearing the human skin-suit, and attempts to drag back down below, before its insidious pressence grows too powerful. Thats why a Sin-Eater with Psyche above 5 must spend some time in the Underworld occationally. </div> </div> </div>Cool theory, though I'm not sure if I agree, but then I'd have to reread through the Geist core again. It is pretty vague or at least not very clear on why a Sin-Eater needs to spend time in the Underworld when Psyche grows... Though I'm sure it's mentioned its to do with needing to keep their connection up with Death energys to upkeep their higher level of connection to it... <i>Or something.</i><br /> <br /> So, anymore thoughts on the subject? I'd like to hear some more theories on the Underworld too. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T19:35:33-07:00","id":442095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/441409-ghosts-and-such?p=442083#post442083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This I suppose asks the question that if a Mage makes a ghost from a living person and they die and have unfinished business... Do they leave behind a ghost for that and now there are two ghosts of the same person?</div> </div> </div> </div>The God-Machine has projects that can split and fuse ghosts, so I don't imagine it's anything like impossible.<br /> <hr /><br /> I've got a particular fascination with the view of the Underworld as the Infinite Reliquary and how that seems to bleed into its residents \u2014 chthonians aren't properly &quot;conscious,&quot; the core of a geist's being is <i>an object</i>, the Junkyard's crushers are basically the Dominion's gods, and there's ambiguity within Mictlan's writeup about whether the prime candidate for resident deathlord is the being with explicit fiat command of its laws or its spouse is, as examples.<br /> <br /> The Dead aren't accustomed to thinking like the Living, and their practice at it fades with quarantine and starvation.<br /> <br /> The Underworld is a place of inversion. Near the borders, the Living become like the Dead, and vice versa. Masks matter more than faces, Vice matters more than Virtue.<br /> <br /> The Dead are tools that wield their wielders.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T21:13:13-07:00","id":442157,"title":"","content":"Mind explaining what you mean by Infinite Reliquary? Its a term I've not really come across and can't find anything on... Though I admit its been a while and memory fails sometimes.<br /> <br /> I do find that Vice has a stronger grasp of beings there, that it can pull someone in and trap them. I'm thinking more of the Tableau when I mention that, which I see as a strange amalgamation of the dead punishing themselves for guilt in some vice... Sort of like being trapped in a loop of self-indulgent suffering?<br /> <br /> I'm not sold on the dead being tools... Despite their uses by Mages and the God-Machine... The more talk about them though does seem to place them as being more astral body taken from a person rather than the person (makes sense that this astral body would get to personify something beyond the person and more based on what purpose it ends up with to, perhaps?). A kind of construction of someone's willpower, in a way (different from the stat, Willpower, you understand). The Underworld to that point seems a place that sucks up those ghosts that would be forgotten. Without anchors to keep them linked to the world of the living, they fall to the Underworld, brushed under the metaphysical carpet, so to speak.<br /> <br /> I'm still puzzled somewhat on the purpose of the Underworld, that it is here the dead end up when their anchors fail and they are slunk further within the longer they are there or for how long they have been dead (based on mechanics for searching for a particular ghost in the Underworld in Book of the Dead, that it takes longer searches if they've been dead longer, along with the penalties for communicating with a Yellow-bones compared to a Cooler).<br /> <br /> Going back on the Cthonians that eat these older sunk-low ghosts and are seemingly maintained by doing so, can a demon from Inferno leave a ghost behind? As I have my own growing thoughts on these creatures...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T21:54:10-07:00","id":442179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/441409-ghosts-and-such?p=442157#post442157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mind explaining what you mean by Infinite Reliquary? Its a term I've not really come across and can't find anything on... Though I admit its been a while and memory fails sometimes.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a phrase culled from VtR: Mythologies's &quot;The Second Death&quot; section that's stuck with me over the years:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Underworld is not truly a \u201cplace\u201d in the sense that most would understand it. It is a kind of Limbo, <b>a vast, perhaps infinite reliquary where ghosts banished from Twilight dwell.</b> Ghosts whose anchors are destroyed, who are exorcised or are destroyed themselves end up in the Underworld. It is not the afterlife, per se: individuals who die and pass on without leaving a ghost behind, or ghosts whose anchors were resolved, allowing them to \u201cmove on,\u201d do not go to the Underworld. Where such souls <u>do</u> go is a mystery. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm not sold on the dead being tools\u2026 </div> </div> </div>I use the wording because &quot;chthonians are Differently Conscious and this appears to be reflected in the way that more alien ghosts behave&quot; is wordier and less straightforward. I'm saying the dead are at their base given over to patterns and that the dead among the Underworld are increasingly rendered uniform and stripped of the means to retain individual personality without effort.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The more talk about them though does seem to place them as being more astral body taken from a person rather than the person (makes sense that this astral body would get to personify something beyond the person and more based on what purpose it ends up with to, perhaps?). A kind of construction of someone's willpower, in a way (different from the stat, Willpower, you understand). The Underworld to that point seems a place that sucks up those ghosts that would be forgotten. Without anchors to keep them linked to the world of the living, they fall to the Underworld, brushed under the metaphysical carpet, so to speak. </div> </div> </div>And anchors are built on memory, which fades in the absence of sustained attachment. Recall that ghosts with anchors <i>can't</i> enter the Underworld, that many things in the Great Below ask for memories as payment, and that the part of the personality described in 2e as a comforting distraction is showcased and strengthened there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T23:29:28-07:00","id":442235,"title":"","content":"So we can say I suppose, that through ghosts then being unable to leave outside of specific circumstances also, that they need Anchors waiting for them back on the other side or they need to Fetter themselves or some other way, it seems like the Underworld is again a place for the restless dead to be swept away. Without the aspects in the world of the living that keeps the ghost remembered and maintained, the memory of it is swallowed to the Underworld.<br /> <br /> I keep coming back to memories because there are Dead Domains in the Lower Depths that seem to house other things forgotten; An-Shot-Ka seems to a domain of lost architecture, The Athenaeum is a library of knowledge lost to the ages and The Grave Dream is where forgotten dreams dwell. Not to mention that Oppia seems to operate on Essence as describing it as a maleable force of rememberance to the dead that maintains the ghosts of the Underworld and The Ocean of Fragments steals away identifiers of those who enter it.<br /> <br /> I am reminded once more through these things of the film <i>Jacob's Ladder</i> and that the dead have their memories and attachments cleaved from them, so they can pass on. If someone is unwilling, it will be like demons are tearing them away, if they have made peace, it's more like angels are guiding the dead.<br /> <br /> Any opinions on where a ghost may Pass On to? If we go with the classical naming conventions of the Underworld from the Geist core, that the Upper Reaches are Erebus and the Lower Depths are Tartarus, via Greek mythology, it seems to hint Elysium would be where the ghosts may go to. Book of the Dead hints more those who lose their identity in the Ocean of Fragments wash up at Stygia as a shade, which is something I find kind of cool, tbh although I'm not sure about that, given the info on the Exarch of Death, The Psychopomp...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T04:56:22-07:00","id":442424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Any opinions on where a ghost may Pass On to? </div> </div> </div>I like it being a kind of illusion. Passing on is simply the ghost finally dying properly.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T07:57:23-07:00","id":442523,"title":"","content":"Some Ghosts are souls, or more specifically removing a persons soul and leaving it alone will transform it into a Ghost. Likewise a Ghost in the Shadow will transform into a Death Spirit so some spirits were once souls too. Purified fuse their minds with their spirit (soul) and become Spirit ascendant ephemeral beings with some uncanny ghostlike qualities.<br /> <br /> For the most part though most Ghosts are psychicish imprints, what is really intriguing though is that in NWoD the actual soul isn't really the end all, be all of the self since you could remove a persons soul and slap in somebody else's soul and they'll still be &quot;I am [same name]&quot; through out the whole process although they'll become a bit... weird from the experience. In fact removing their soul simply causes them to lose their will to live not their sense of self.<br /> <br /> My own head cannon pet theory is that Ghosts are the &quot;I&quot; in &quot;I am, therefore I am&quot; from the mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2111-doeman","name":"DoeMan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T09:48:48-07:00","id":442703,"title":"","content":"*nods* It seems fair enough that a Soul is what gives the person a will to live and is seperate from a Ghost, though as mentioned, a Soul may become a Ghost (though that may be related close to death... The person's will dies away and leaves behind the psychic imprint of a restless ghost). I didn't know a Ghost that is within the Shadow would become a Death Spirit though, thats a new one on me. Ghosts and Spirits are closely related though, by being ephemeral things, so eh... Seems legit I suppose.<br /> <br /> Purified I see as those shamans that were successful in the ritual that may otherwise create an Ulgan Lineaged Promethean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T22:02:49-07:00","id":443731,"title":"","content":"The &quot;native&quot; realms of the phenomenal world have a universal quality of being... corrupting for lack of a better way to put it; exerting it's influence and by doing so change those who live within them fundamentally to match itself, likewise the ephemeral natives of the phenomenal (specifically Astral, Shadow, Underworld) are very plastic and change naturally by their natures even though how they change is different. With these two qualities combined you pluck one native and plop it in another realm it will change to something else, for a Ghost it will become a Spirit in the Shadow.<br /> <br /> At least that's how I figured this works. Keep in mind that these changes don't usually go both ways, once a Ghost is a Death Spirit it stays a Death Spirit if you put it back in the Underworld. Neither would they usually change into the inhabitants of the realm, a Spirit of anything but Death will go mad and become Magath if it was put in the Underworld (or maybe something else...).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2111-doeman","user":"DoeMan","date":". 03-16-2015, 01:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2111-doeman","name":"DoeMan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T22:35:37-07:00","id":443751,"title":"","content":"DoeMan is taking speculation as fact, I'll note; the bit in question shows up in the Rumors section of the Mockingbird's entry in Night Horrors: Wolfsbane:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> While the event described above is extremely rare, it is possible for a human who dies in the Shadow to leave behind a ghost trapped in the Shadow. Such a ghost automatically possesses the Material Vision Numen, and may learn Numina that allow it to consume Essence like a spirit. A ghost in the Shadow cannot be exorcised, nor can it be banished by destroying its anchors \u2014 something about the Gauntlet prevents the ghost from moving on. Over time, it might well mutate into some sort of ghost-spirit magath, a blasphemy seldom seen since Father Wolf\u2019s death. What effect that might have on the Shadow around such a creature is anyone\u2019s guess. </div> </div> </div>Elsewhere, in Lodges: the Splintered, the Lodge of Hungry Ghosts contains this tidbit about the ephemeral structure of Japan:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Similarly weird, some spirit hierarchies seem to include yurei (or ghosts). While departed spirits cannot cross over to the Shadow and exist only in Twilight, the Forsaken often find spirits and ghosts communing in various inexplicable ceremonies. </div> </div> </div>The Shadow is actually remarkably efficient as otherworlds go; the primary sources of corruption stem from direct spiritual action or occult vectors like the various strains of disease, rather than simple prolonged exposure like in the Hedge, the Underworld, or the Dreamtime.<br /> <br /> I'm pretty sure that's on account of how visitors to the <i>Hisil</i> aren't usually traipsing around in the backyard of the gods.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T02:56:36-07:00","id":443964,"title":"","content":"Okay... So moving to the Sin-Eaters themselves now... Would it fair to say that they are simply a fetter/anchor for a Geist to escape the Underworld and be a part of the land of the living again? I think there's something more to them than simply wanting a meat-suit, because if that was the case they wouldn't seem so angered when the Sin-Eater causes a sin to Synergy and drops it. They don't want to have a bond with one of the Wretched. I know acting within a Threshold or having a ghost Pass On boosts their Plasm, the latter being a nice little reward to not simply punch a ghost to the Underworld (or destroying them, which pisses the Geist off for obvious reasons), whilst taking plasm from a Deathmask seems to be a sin against Synergy, for some reason.<br /> <br /> Another thing I don't understand (which may be to do with the wording within the book) about high-level Psyche is, if their connection to death energy is so sensitive (which to me reads they can pick it up and react to it much easier), then why the need to go to the Underworld to keep the connection strong? I'd say that would be more for someone with less control of the plasm within them, right? I get it's a mechanical thing to have a con for higher Power-stat, same as all the lines have something, but I'm not clicking with it...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T13:34:31-07:00","id":444842,"title":"","content":"Well Geists have managed to, in the process of becoming whatever they are, escape the normal bounds of standard Ghosts and don't need an anchor to escape the Underworld (until they reach Rank 6... maybe). In fact they need their anchors to keep themselves from passing on, if they need to keep themselves in the material world they merely have to do what Spirits do,promote itself and it's influences which generally translates to unusual streaks of inexplicable deaths of the same type in an area.<br /> EDIT: The God Machine Chronicles rules update actually explains it a bit for the Ghost section in the rules update.<br /> <br /> The thing about life in NWoD is that it is very addictive to Ghosts, they crave life and to live and Geists can experience being alive by becoming Sin-Eaters with a suitable candidate. Beyond that they all universally have an obsession based around their archetypes and enjoy pursuing these desires when being &quot;alive&quot; again. Finally their nuts, and some Synergy breaches is an irrational distrust on the Geist's part and for others not even the Geist knows why it's a breach it just is.<br /> <br /> For that last one, this is probably most likely tied to the fact that Sin-Eaters are not really human anymore their half-Ghost hybrids and one quirk with the Underworld is that the older and more powerful a Ghost is the more it &quot;sinks&quot; deeper and deeper within. This pull is the same thing tugging away at the Sin-Eater.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2111-doeman","user":"DoeMan","date":". 03-16-2015, 04:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2111-doeman","name":"DoeMan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T15:47:34-07:00","id":445021,"title":"","content":"The way I run things, Sin-Eaters at Psyche 6 and above effectively become quasi-ghost-like themselves. Its not that they have to keep the connection strong, its that the connection has become so strong that the same entropic force that forces ghosts inexhorably down into the great darkness, pulls the Sin-Eater down aswell. If the Sin-Eater doesn't willfully abide by the &quot;time spend in Underworld&quot; rule, he'll randomly fade into the ground and be dragged down into the Underworld. All the more violently at higher Psyche ratings.<br /> <br /> Geister are sorta like minor Gods of very specific kinds of death. They're kinda a thinking idea of death, more so than an actual entity. Though they still carry the memory of the person they once were, they aren't really that person anymore. They're that persons ephemeral ideas, memories and emotions shaped by whatever aspect of death that dominated his psyche. Almost like an unliving self-perpetuating Zeigeist of death.<br /> Now enter the Sin-Eater. An idea is no good if nobody believes that idea. A Ghost will fade if forgotten and so will even the most intricate idea. Most Ghosts dont really have any insurance that they wont suddenly disppear, because their last Anchor is destroyed. The Geist however, as a pretty good foothold. Its become an idea, almost universally so. A Geist of &quot;Fiery Death&quot; or &quot;Mass Shootings&quot; probably wont loose that Anchor anytime soon. However, just because it wont lose that Anchor doesn't mean its happy to just stagnate. Ideas need to propagate in order to expand, and a dead man wants to be alive again. The Geist is the merger between an idea and a dead-man, so it is natural that this thing has two priorities: Propagate the idea that is ME, and experience life.<br /> Although it is grosely hindered in both of these in its form, it can enlist a mortal agent to accomplish both for it, doing both vicariously through the Sin-Eater.<br /> In this regard, the Sin-Eater isn't just a meat-suit for the dead-man to experience life again. The Sin-Eater is also the living conduit of the very idea and notion of whatever death the Geist embodies. Every Sin-Eater is the high-priest and ultimate authority in the orthodoxy that is their Geist. When the Sin-Eater transgresses against Stnergy, he is going against the dogma of his religion. A shame to him, that this particular religion has its God living inside his mind and soul. It is an angry God.<br /> Worse still, that God doesn't just live there. Its melted with him, becomming something half-way between an idea, a dead-man and a living person. Synergy is a measure of how well that trinity is balanced. While both the Sin-Eater and Geist has a loose understaning of their part of the amalgamations mind, none of them truely understand the mix-thing they've become, and the extend to which their identity as an idea as come to define them. Therefor, they might each believe that a certain action is entirely within reason, but its still a Synergy sin, because it goes against the morality of the amalgamation they've become, which neither of them understand.<br /> <br /> Well. Thats enough spit-balling for now.<br /> Tl;DR: Geists are Gods of Death and Sin-Eaters are their high priests. They dont like transgressing against their Gods dogma.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T18:00:56-07:00","id":445121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/441409-ghosts-and-such?p=443964#post443964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay... So moving to the Sin-Eaters themselves now... Would it fair to say that they are simply a fetter/anchor for a Geist to escape the Underworld and be a part of the land of the living again?</div> </div> </div> </div>Got a thing about that, actually:<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/113788-ghosts-and-possession?p=113914#post113914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Geist would be a mid-high Rank ghost which went for Influence over a thematic form of death, and picked up the Manifestation that lets it make a Sin-Eater.<br /> <br /> That Manifestation isn't written up, and might not be even if Geist ever gets a GMC update, but that's the design intention. Think of it as a cross, mechanically, between Claim and the Strix &quot;Synthesis&quot; power, which is the one the owls use to &quot;embrace&quot; new vampires. Sin-Eaters aren't &quot;ghost Claimed&quot; - they're a major template, not a minor one - but that's the general notion.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think there's something more to them than simply wanting a meat-suit, because if that was the case they wouldn't seem so angered when the Sin-Eater causes a sin to Synergy and drops it. They don't want to have a bond with one of the Wretched. I know acting within a Threshold or having a ghost Pass On boosts their Plasm, the latter being a nice little reward to not simply punch a ghost to the Underworld (or destroying them, which pisses the Geist off for obvious reasons), whilst taking plasm from a Deathmask seems to be a sin against Synergy, for some reason. </div> </div> </div>Synergy seems likely to get treated similarly to Harmony in 2e; getting closer to death puts you nearer to the 0 end, and that's explicit in the text of a lot of discord triggers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Another thing I don't understand (which may be to do with the wording within the book) about high-level Psyche is, if their connection to death energy is so sensitive (which to me reads they can pick it up and react to it much easier), then why the need to go to the Underworld to keep the connection strong? I'd say that would be more for someone with less control of the plasm within them, right? I get it's a mechanical thing to have a con for higher Power-stat, same as all the lines have something, but I'm not clicking with it... </div> </div> </div>Plasm is a binding agent and larger constructions tend to be easier to fuck up structurally. The Underworld both provides a potential drip-feed of the stuff and has more permissive laws of physics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T18:39:08-07:00","id":445157,"title":"","content":"I dunno about Synergy sins coming from the Sin-Eater going against spreading the idea of the Geist or doing what it wants to be done now it's up top-side properly. The main Synergy sins are for destroying things related to death, sure (along with bringing the dead back)... But not something like saying 'No' to your Geist. Infact going about and spreading death en masse are hefty Synergy sins, only a single specific planned murder avoids the Synergy sins. Do it as a serial spree or a mass killing, then the Geist is gonna be pissed. Keep doing it and it's a quick way to end up as one of the Wretched, past the Sin-Eater trying to kill themselves or the Geist they're bound to. I get the idea of the Geist trying to keep it's Influence alive as a kind of pseudo-anchor, though the mechanics do not support it as a notion, really.<br /> <br /> I reminded myself Geists are annoyed by taking Plasm from a Deathmask mainly because Deathmasks are the 'corpses' of other Geist.<br /> <br /> Having the Sin-Eater become somewhat more ghost-like themself and feeling the pull of the Underworld from being more sensitive to the ways of death makes alot of sense for why they need to pop down there every now and then at higher Psyche levels. I don't think it was written so well in Core, perhaps that's something Geist v2 can sort out, if it happens to come out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T02:05:59-07:00","id":445506,"title":"","content":"Well, if the pants dont fit, you get a new pair of pants. If your local shop dont sell any pants you like, you make some yourself.<br /> In Geists case, I generally try to homebrew alot of mechanics in an attempt to make the mechanics alot in line with the thematic focus. I think we can all agree that Geists mechanics got borked somewhere along production, but I still feel like the thematic focus and fluff stuff is some of the strongest in WoD. Therefor, I dont think we should nessesarily contrain ourselves by saying &quot;The mechanics dont support it&quot;, as a means to justify why a thing cant be as suggested.<br /> <br /> If I was to try to justify the &quot;mass killings is a Synergy trigger&quot; along the lines of my previous &quot;Geister are death-gods/death-ideas&quot; kinda thing, I would say that stems from the discord between the part of the Geist thats still human. Even if the Geist has become an amalgamation between a dead-man and an idea, that dead-man still has a certain degreee of morality left. He might not be overly happy with ruthlessly killing an entire family, because one of them stepped on your shoes in line to the shopping mall.<br /> However, if the Geist agrees that its a good idea, and its in line with the Geist nature as a Death god/idea, then I dont see why you couldn't carry over the &quot;Changing Morality Code&quot; from Hunter, to reflect the Sin-Eater and Geist comming to a closer understanding of each other, albietly to the detriment of the Sin-Eaters humanity.<br /> I've already implemented this system in my own Geist game, and it was recieved rather positively.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T14:39:51-07:00","id":446546,"title":"","content":"Tbh, as things are developing, if Geist does it's second edition, I see Synergy being changed or better explained to show the degree of Flesh and Ghost, likely in a similar manner to Werewolf second edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}